    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "polxrnw",
      "content": "The calorific value of a fuel is defined as:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tbpkwmc",
      "content": "A) Heat produced by burning 1 kg of fuel completely"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vk3frn9",
      "content": "B) Heat required to burn 1 kg of fuel"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0if9651",
      "content": "C) Temperature at which fuel burns"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "k1i5j15",
      "content": "D) Efficiency of fuel"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "9gjcqg7",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: A"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fyv51ki",
      "content": "<br></br>Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qlztfvc",
      "content": "Calorific value is the amount of heat produced when 1 kg of fuel is completely burnt."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7khr3t4",
      "content": "Unit: kJ/kg."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jbzsyfa",
      "content": "Higher calorific value means better fuel."
    },
    {
      "id": "xhdvt73",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q2."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j4w0k0r",
      "content": "Solar cells work on the principle of:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "scy6vzg",
      "content": "A) Photoelectric effect"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "xj2cjee",
      "content": "B) Photovoltaic effect"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "xrjwkrl",
      "content": "C) Electromagnetic induction"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "sxay9p4",
      "content": "D) Thermal radiation"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "mhvm5ct",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: B"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5jc7o63",
      "content": "<br></br>Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "spc5jsr",
      "content": "Solar cells convert sunlight directly into electricity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kt45ap2",
      "content": "They work on the photovoltaic effect."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "MCQs",
      "id": "rrm5peg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qnl8fpu",
      "content": "Silicon semiconductor is commonly used."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ltvv3bh",
      "content": "They produce DC electricity."
    },
    {
      "id": "j1d6qul",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q3."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q67jzga",
      "content": "The ultimate source of most energy on Earth is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "k929c62",
      "content": "A) Moon"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2hfk5gh",
      "content": "B) Coal"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "m1diisn",
      "content": "C) Sun"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4w3qcpm",
      "content": "D) Nuclear reaction"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ff28ik6",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cg2irww",
      "content": "<br></br>Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0kqbxx3",
      "content": "Wind energy, hydro energy and fossil fuels indirectly depend on solar energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uzt4idl",
      "content": "Hence, Sun is the ultimate source of most energy on Earth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8d3zpwr",
      "content": "Tidal energy depends on Moon’s gravitational pull."
    },
    {
      "id": "5auxjb5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q4."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zjc4tj1",
      "content": "Nuclear power plants generate electricity using:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8denjvq",
      "content": "A) Nuclear fusion"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "kkje4sm",
      "content": "B) Chemical reaction"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "6wh14az",
      "content": "C) Nuclear fission"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ia86rxf",
      "content": "D) Combustion"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4t7bou0",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h9lyzvj",
      "content": "<br></br>Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "30et4mn",
      "content": "In nuclear power plants, heavy nuclei like Uranium-235 undergo fission."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5eu0uob",
      "content": "Large amount of energy is released (E = mc²)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8803vst",
      "content": "Controlled chain reaction occurs inside nuclear reactor."
    },
    {
      "id": "45inr8a",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q5."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s0ixd6r",
      "content": "For efficient generation of wind energy, minimum wind speed should be approximately:"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Multiple-choice questions form a major portion of competitive examinations.",
        "Always verify all choices before selecting the final option in MCQ sections."
      ],
      "id": "7xt1s34"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "6u9mcww",
      "content": "A) 5 km/h"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "vgg5ri8",
      "content": "B) 10 km/h"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "pbkqqxa",
      "content": "C) 15 km/h"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "zsatgnf",
      "content": "D) 25 km/h"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "s1dfc7p",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wus7o6d",
      "content": "<br></br>Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "njce3em",
      "content": "Wind turbines require minimum wind speed of about 15 km/h to operate efficiently."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q7b9npe",
      "content": "Below this speed, electricity generation is not economical."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7zmr2i1",
      "content": "Wind energy is renewable but intermittent."
    }
  ],
